(Architecture and state model) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
48 725 Td
(Request flow: independent Erlang CLI OS process -> httpc -> HTTP/JSON -> inets:httpd request) Tj
T*
(callback -> reddit_server gen_server -> reddit_engine pure state transition -> JSON) Tj
T*
(response.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(reddit_sup supervises the authoritative engine server. Its serialized transitions keep post) Tj
T*
(IDs, votes, scores, karma, memberships, messages, and signatures consistent. HTTP connection) Tj
T*
(processes call the same engine with a five-second timeout.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each CLI uses only REST for user operations. The demo prints client OS PIDs and launches) Tj
T*
(concurrent clients to exercise shared server state. There is no Erlang distribution) Tj
T*
(requirement for REST clients.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Engine state uses indexed maps for users, communities, subscriptions, posts, community) Tj
T*
(posts, comments, thread relationships, votes, and inboxes. All content receives increasing) Tj
T*
(global IDs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The server defaults to 127.0.0.1:8080. Address, port, and base/bonus mode are configurable.) Tj
T*
(inets supervises the HTTP service. Engine state is intentionally in memory; server or engine) Tj
T*
(restart loses data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Identity follows the existing engine: clients supply trusted X-User usernames. Registration) Tj
T*
(needs no password. Caller checks protect operations relative to that supplied identity; this) Tj
T*
(is not real authentication.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The implementation adds case-insensitive Unicode substring search over post text and) Tj
T*
(community names, community listing, and single-post retrieval to support an end-to-end) Tj
T*
(demonstration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
