/F1 10 Tf
12 TL
48 725 Td
(Install Erlang/OTP 27+ with compiler, development headers, EUnit, inets, public_key, and) Tj
T*
(crypto. Put escript on PATH. The scripts/project4 launcher also recognizes a user-local) Tj
T*
(Erlang installation. Use Python 3 only for report/package commands.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Build and run: ./scripts/project4 build; ./scripts/project4 test; ./scripts/project4 server) Tj
T*
(--mode base. Use separate terminals for Alice and Bob.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Alice: ./scripts/project4 client --user alice --verbose register alice; then create erlang;) Tj
T*
(then post erlang "Hello REST" using the same client prefix.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Bob: register bob; join erlang; feed; search REST; vote post 1 1. Alice or Bob can inspect) Tj
T*
(karma alice. Comments support arbitrary nesting via parent IDs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Use --url http://127.0.0.1:8081 for another port. The interactive shell accepts JSON arrays) Tj
T*
(of command arguments, such as ["feed"] or ["post","erlang","Hello"].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Automated multi-process demos: ./scripts/project4 demo base and ./scripts/project4 demo) Tj
T*
(bonus. Each starts a fresh ephemeral server, launches independent client OS processes, runs) Tj
T*
(all supported features, and asserts concurrent repeated votes preserve karma one.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Server logs include request ID, method, path, username, status, and elapsed microseconds.) Tj
T*
(Verbose clients print the actual HTTP method/URL and returned status/JSON, including) Tj
T*
(matching request IDs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(docs/VIDEO_GUIDE.md contains a timed approximately five-minute main demo, exact commands and) Tj
T*
(expected IDs, narration, a separate bonus walkthrough, and recording/upload instructions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
